course: dictionary
lesson: 12646
title: Displeased: a polite way to say annoyed
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Displeased means annoyed or unhappy about something someone has done. It is a polite, rather formal word, so you will often meet it in stories about kings, queens, teachers and parents. «The queen was most displeased when the guests arrived late.» The word tells you she was not happy, but it does not shout about it.
explain: Displeased is often followed by with, at or about, as in «displeased with». Look at the words around it to find the reason. In «The teacher was displeased with our noisy work», the clue is the noisy work, which tells you what made her unhappy.
explain: Displeased is also the past form of the verb displease, which means to make someone annoyed or unhappy. «The rain displeased the picnic guests.» Here the rain made them unhappy. Watch for the word not: «He was not displeased» means he was secretly quite pleased.
fact: Displeased means annoyed or unhappy about something someone has done.
fact: «Displeased» is a polite, rather formal word, and a gentle way to say angry.
fact: Displeased is often followed by with, at or about, as in «displeased with».
fact: «Not displeased» means secretly quite pleased.
fact: Displease is the verb; displeased is its past form, and it can also work as an adjective.
exercise: «The queen was most displeased when the guests arrived late.» What does displeased mean? | Very tired from walking | Lost and confused | Delighted and dancing | *Annoyed or unhappy about something
exercise: «He was not displeased with his test score.» What does this suggest? | He was very angry | He was lost | *He was secretly quite pleased | He did not take the test
exercise: «Dad looked displeased when the dog dug up the garden.» Find and copy the one word that shows Dad was annoyed. | looked | garden | dug | *displeased
test: «The rain displeased the picnic guests.» In this sentence, displeased means: | *Made them feel annoyed or unhappy | Made them feel sleepy | Made them dance | Made them feel excited
test: Which word is a gentle, formal way to say someone is angry? | *Displeased | Furious | Sleepy | Delighted
exam: Which sentence shows the king was secretly quite pleased? | The king was displeased with the gift. | *The king was not displeased with the gift. | The king was displeased, so he cried.
